course: dictionary
lesson: 8623
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word scripture is a good example. It can mean the holy writings of the Bible, or the holy writings of any religion. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Jesus was tempted by the devil and said no each time, answering with Scripture» tells you the holy writings of the Bible, because Jesus is quoting them. «Sikh scripture teaches seeing all people as equal» tells you scripture can also mean the holy writings of another religion. Look for clue words such as Christian, Sikh, Bible or Qur'an.
explain: Scripture can also mean an old school subject where pupils studied the Bible. Today that lesson is called Religious Education. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Scripture means the holy writings of a religion.
fact: For Christians, Scripture means the holy writings of the Bible.
fact: «Holy Scripture» and «a passage of scripture» are common phrases.
fact: Scripture was once a school subject in UK schools, and it is now called Religious Education.
fact: «Lent» remembers the forty days Jesus spent in the desert, when he said no to temptation using Scripture.
exercise: «Jesus was tempted by the devil and said no each time, answering with Scripture.» In this sentence, what does Scripture mean? | A prayer said before a meal | *The holy writings of the Bible | A church tune sung on Sundays | A school lesson for Bible study
exercise: «Sikh scripture teaches seeing all people as equal.» What does scripture mean here? | The holy writings of the Bible | A short story about a dog | A church tune sung on Sundays | *The holy writings of the Sikh religion
exercise: Scripture was once a school subject in the UK. What is it called now? | *Religious Education | Design and Technology | Physical Education | Music
test: «In religious education, Christians read Scripture in church services.» Which holy writings are these? | The Vedas | *The Bible | The Torah | The Qur'an
test: Which phrase from the lessons uses scripture to mean holy writings? | a scripture of cheese | scripture-coloured paint | *quote Scripture | scripture on wheels
exam: The vicar says Scripture leaves some mystery about a lie told in panic. Which holy writings is the vicar talking about? | *Christianity, the Bible | Gardening, with seeds | Football, with rules | Cooking, with recipes
